1
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:51,000
One Band. One Dream. One Summer.

2
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Satisfaction is a comedy, music, romance film directed by Joan Freeman.

3
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:21,000
When a young rock group called The Mystery gets its first gig at a
club, it's an opportunity to see what life is all about.

4
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Fresh out of high school, the rockers are hired by an exclusive
beach resort thanks to a faded '60s songwriter.

5
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:51,000
There, they meet with romance and adventure.

6
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:36,000
But street-smart lead singer Jennie Lee faces a dilemma:
pursue her budding career or finish high school.

7
00:40:15,000 --> 00:40:21,000
Jennie Lee, played by Justine Bateman.

8
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:06,000
Martin Falcon, played by Liam Neeson.

9
00:51:45,000 --> 00:51:51,000
Mooch, played by Trini Alvarado.

10
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
Nickie, played by Scott Coffey.

11
01:03:15,000 --> 01:03:21,000
Billy, played by Britta Phillips.

12
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
Daryle, played by Julia Roberts.

13
01:14:45,000 --> 01:14:51,000
Satisfaction (also titled Girls of Summer) is a 1988 American comedy-drama film
directed by Joan Freeman and starring Justine Bateman and Liam Neeson.

14
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:36,000
Primarily known today as Julia Roberts' first credited big-screen role, Satisfaction is also one
of the few theatrical productions by either Aaron Spelling or the NBC network.

15
01:26:15,000 --> 01:26:21,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
